 Mateo, United States.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Angela L. Kleiman | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $5.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Essex Property Trust, Inc. is a large-cap real estate business with a $19.4B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically. Gross margins of 70% confirm genuine pricing power.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 3.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 147% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.4692309411685371},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 25% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","30 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Real Estate sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"DoGo Power p\u0159edstavila na GENERA 2026 v Madridu ukldn energie (ESS) podporujc tvorbu inteligentnch st","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/dogo-power-pedstavila-na-genera-2026-v-madridu-ukladani-energie-ess-podporujici-tvorbu-inteligentnich-siti-302951613.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795766760.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"DoGo Power \u0434\u0435\u043c\u043e\u043d\u0441\u0442\u0440\u0438\u0440\u0443\u0435\u0442 Smart Grid-Forming ESS \u043d\u0430 \u0432\u044b\u0441\u0442\u0430\u0432\u043a\u0435 GENERA 2026 Madrid","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/dogo-p